From 6bb09d40075012ab287c9599489f1fbc84a269b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 01:43:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/52] ppc32: define LiftoffAssembler::emit_i32_muli
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

G5 build error #7b of the 12.4 port (mksnapshot link, 98%):

  Undefined symbols for architecture ppc:
    v8::internal::wasm::LiftoffAssembler::emit_i32_muli(Register,
    Register, int), referenced from:
      LiftoffCompiler::CallIndirect(...) in liftoff-compiler.cc.o

New class for this port: 32-bit-only Liftoff hooks.  liftoff-assembler.h
declares emit_i32_muli for every backend and emit_ptrsize_muli resolves
to it when kSystemPointerSize == 4; the arm, ia32 and riscv32 backends
each define it, the ppc backend (64-bit-only upstream) never did, so
the call from CallIndirect's table-slot scaling had no definition on
ppc32.  Define it next to emit_i64_muli in the same shape: power-of-two
immediates become a shift, everything else goes through r0 + MulS32
(whose trailing extsw is PPC64-gated by patch 0004).  Guarded
!V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 so the ppc64 build is untouched.

Compile-reachable, runtime-dead here: Liftoff bails on ppc32 (patch
0030), so this only has to exist and be correct.

Class sweep (scratchpad liftoffaudit.py — names defined by BOTH arm
and ia32 backends, minus the ppc backend's definitions under a ppc32
guard view; macro-list entries expanded): exactly one missing name,
this one.  Nothing arm-only is referenced from the generic Liftoff
sources either.  The mksnapshot link listed no other Liftoff symbol,
consistent with that.
---
 .../baseline/ppc/liftoff-assembler-ppc-inl.h     | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/wasm/baseline/ppc/liftoff-assembler-ppc-inl.h b/v8/src/wasm/baseline/ppc/liftoff-assembler-ppc-inl.h
index f9a3f4f..0023676 100644
--- a/v8/src/wasm/baseline/ppc/liftoff-assembler-ppc-inl.h
+++ b/v8/src/wasm/baseline/ppc/liftoff-assembler-ppc-inl.h
@@ -1969,6 +1969,22 @@ void LiftoffAssembler::emit_i64_muli(LiftoffRegister dst, LiftoffRegister lhs,
   MulS64(dst.gp(), lhs.gp(), r0);
 }
 
+#if !V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
+// Every 32-bit backend (arm, ia32, riscv32) defines this; the ppc backend
+// upstream is 64-bit-only and never needed it, but emit_ptrsize_muli
+// resolves to it when kSystemPointerSize == 4 (CallIndirect's table-slot
+// scaling in liftoff-compiler.cc), so ppc32 fails to link without it.
+// Same shape as emit_i64_muli above.
+void LiftoffAssembler::emit_i32_muli(Register dst, Register lhs, int32_t imm) {
+  if (base::bits::IsPowerOfTwo(imm)) {
+    emit_i32_shli(dst, lhs, base::bits::WhichPowerOfTwo(imm));
+    return;
+  }
+  mov(r0, Operand(imm));
+  MulS32(dst, lhs, r0);
+}
+#endif  // !V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
+
 bool LiftoffAssembler::emit_select(LiftoffRegister dst, Register condition,
                                    LiftoffRegister true_value,
                                    LiftoffRegister false_value,
